@page "/docs/cli"
@layout DocsLayout
@using MudBlazor

<PageTitle>CLI Guide — AgentBlazor Docs</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-article">
    <section class="docs-hero">
        <p class="docs-hero__eyebrow">CLI Guide</p>
        <h1 class="docs-hero__title">Preview first, apply second, validate after.</h1>
        <p class="docs-hero__lede">
            The CLI exists to take an existing Blazor app through a predictable onboarding path instead of making you infer
            the required AgentBlazor wiring by hand.
        </p>

        <div class="docs-chip-row">
            <span><code>init</code> generates <code>.agentblazor/AGENT.md</code> and state</span>
            <span><code>scaffold</code> previews before mutating files</span>
            <span><code>doctor</code> checks readiness</span>
            <span><code>validate</code> checks install state and scaffold audit trail</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>Install and update</h2>
                <p>The tool is published as a prerelease global tool today.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <pre class="docs-code"><code>dotnet tool install --global AgentBlazor.Cli --version 0.1.0-preview.9
dotnet tool update --global AgentBlazor.Cli --version 0.1.0-preview.9</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>Standard run order</h2>
                <p>This is the canonical command flow for an existing Blazor app.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <pre class="docs-code"><code>agentblazor init ./MySolution.slnx --host MyBlazorApp
agentblazor scaffold ./MySolution.slnx --host MyBlazorApp --provider openai
agentblazor scaffold ./MySolution.slnx --host MyBlazorApp --provider openai --diff
agentblazor scaffold ./MySolution.slnx --host MyBlazorApp --provider openai --approve
agentblazor doctor ./MySolution.slnx --host MyBlazorApp
agentblazor validate ./MySolution.slnx --host MyBlazorApp</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>Command reference</h2>
                <p>The current CLI surface is install-focused, not a general project generator.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-definition-grid">
            <div class="docs-definition">
                <strong><code>init</code></strong>
                <p>Generates <code>.agentblazor/AGENT.md</code> and <code>.agentblazor/state.json</code>, then prints the exact next commands.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-definition">
                <strong><code>scaffold</code></strong>
                <p>Previews the baseline install plan. Use <code>--approve</code> to apply it and <code>--diff</code> for file-level diff output.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-definition">
                <strong><code>doctor</code></strong>
                <p>Checks package references, runtime registration, endpoint mapping, shell assets, layout providers, and chat mounting.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-definition">
                <strong><code>validate</code></strong>
                <p>Combines readiness checks with scaffold manifest verification and tracked-file audit checks when a manifest exists.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-definition">
                <strong><code>update</code></strong>
                <p>Refreshes the agent-facing project summary after code changes.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-definition">
                <strong><code>watch</code></strong>
                <p>Runs continuous refresh during development.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>Provider selection</h2>
                <p>Provider registration can now be scaffolded directly into the host startup path.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <pre class="docs-code"><code>agentblazor scaffold ./MySolution.slnx --host MyBlazorApp --provider openai
agentblazor scaffold ./MySolution.slnx --host MyBlazorApp --provider azure-openai
agentblazor scaffold ./MySolution.slnx --host MyBlazorApp --provider ollama</code></pre>

        <div class="docs-note">
            <strong>Azure OpenAI:</strong> scaffold writes <code>AzureOpenAI:Endpoint</code>, <code>AzureOpenAI:DeploymentName</code>,
            and <code>AzureOpenAI:ApiKey</code> lookups. Apps using managed identity can replace the API key argument with a
            <code>TokenCredential</code>.
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>Host-shape behavior</h2>
                <p><code>scaffold</code> now changes behavior depending on whether the host is standard, supported-but-advanced, or unclassifiable.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-card-grid">
            <div class="docs-card">
                <strong>Standard Blazor Web App</strong>
                <p>The CLI can patch package references, <code>Program.cs</code>, <code>App.razor</code>, layout, starter workflow, and a chat entry page.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-card">
                <strong>Hosted WebAssembly server + client</strong>
                <p>The CLI can infer the companion client project from project references, patch standard server startup wiring, and patch safe client files.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-card">
                <strong>Recognizable advanced hosts</strong>
                <p>Legacy server hosts and other custom Blazor shapes stay review-first. Safe additions still apply, but risky host wiring becomes guided manual review.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-card">
                <strong>Unclassified hosts</strong>
                <p>The CLI stops early rather than guessing at startup or shell wiring that could break the app.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>What a good run looks like</h2>
                <p>Use this as the quick acceptance checklist when testing on a real project.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-check-grid">
            <div class="docs-check">
                <strong>Before apply</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li><code>scaffold</code> previews the expected file set.</li>
                    <li><code>--diff</code> shows startup, shell, layout, and workflow edits that make sense for the host.</li>
                    <li>Provider registration matches the selected <code>--provider</code> flag.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-check">
                <strong>After apply</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li><code>doctor</code> reports the baseline runtime wiring.</li>
                    <li><code>validate</code> passes install checks or reports only expected review-first guidance.</li>
                    <li>The app renders the chat surface and the runtime responds.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-note">
            <strong>The CLI is intentionally not doing everything:</strong> it does not invent provider secrets, environment-specific config,
            or arbitrary startup edits in host shapes it cannot classify safely.
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>Read next</h2>
                <p>Follow the install path into host-shape guidance or troubleshooting.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-next-grid">
            <a href="/docs/hosting-models" class="docs-next-card">
                <strong>Hosting Models</strong>
                <p>Understand when scaffold fully patches, stays review-first, or blocks.</p>
            </a>
            <a href="/docs/troubleshooting" class="docs-next-card">
